WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start position:0%
- It's deeply anti-intellectual
and it's frankly racist.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.204
I think we should call it out

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.705
for what it is.
- It's racist.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.508
- If you look at the kind of
white supremacist ideology

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:11.378
of the 1950s, which
we all denounce,

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.313
it has the same categorization

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the critical race
theory ideology of today.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:18.518 align:start size:84% position:16%
You reduce people
to a racial essence.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.688
Back then and today, it's
whiteness and blackness.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
You create a group
identity-based hierarchy.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, it's different,
but it's the same concept.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.396
And then these critical
race theory trainings

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.930 align:start size:81% position:19%
are essentially
denouncing people,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.033 align:start size:88% position:13%
not on their individual
characteristics,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.035
but on their inborn identity.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
This is something that
was wrong in 1950,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's wrong today, and we
should be very on high alert

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.510
and we should all
be working together

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.512
to jettison this ideology.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.081
(somber music)

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.220 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin, and
this is "The Rubin Report"

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.823 line:0%
As always, guys, make
sure you're subscribed

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.224 line:0%
on our YouTube channel

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
and have that notification
bell clicked on.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.563
And joining me today
is a research fellow

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.365
at the Discovery Institute's

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:08.535 align:start size:84% position:16%
Center on Wealth,
Poverty, &amp; Morality,

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:11.104
and contributing editor
at the "City Journal,"

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.605
and perhaps more importantly,

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:16.509
Mr. Critical Race Theory
himself, Christopher Rufo.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.611
Welcome to the Rubin Report.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.447
- It's great to be with you.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.714
- What do you think
about that title,

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.751
Mr. Critical Race Theory?

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.820 line:0%
- (laughing) I think it's
a little bit misleading,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.922 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
because I think a
lot of the proponents

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.658 line:0%
of critical race theory
would disagree with that.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:35.361
They would say I'm kind of Mr.
Anti-CRT more than anything.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.030
(both laughing)

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:88% position:13%
- All right, well,
we're gonna discuss that

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:43.169
for the next half hour and then
we'll let the people decide.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.405 align:start size:84% position:16%
So really why I
wanted to have you on

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:49.175
is you're one of the people,
at least in the Twitter world,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.144
although now you've
made it to Tucker,

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.279
so that's a nice bump,

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:88% position:13%
that has been explaining
critical race theory

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.253
clearly and honestly and openly.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:03.189 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it is a set of ideas that
basically has infiltrated

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:07.127 align:start size:97% position:3%
almost every part of society
and has so much to do

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:88% position:13%
with why we're seeing
such chaos at the moment

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:13.233
and why everybody is sort of
picking their set of facts

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start position:0%
or their worldview, and we
can't come together on anything.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.872 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I really wanna just
unpack all of that with you

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.174 align:start position:0%
so that my audience can
understand it a little bit more

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.942
because I think when you
say critical race theory,

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.044 align:start size:84% position:16%
people don't know
exactly what it means,

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a lot of different
definitions, all that.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
So just one thing quickly
before we do that,

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.684
which is how did
you get involved

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.720
in all of this in
the first place,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then we'll
take it from there.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.857 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, I've been reporting
the last two years

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
on homelessness,
addiction, mental illness,

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.694 align:start size:84% position:16%
and kind of West
Coast street disorder.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.663
So this has been a
bit of a departure.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:47.167
But it all started when I
got the whistleblower email

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
that said, hey,
the City of Seattle

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.738 align:start position:0%
is now holding racially
segregated diversity trainings,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the segregated system
for white employees

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.543 align:start size:88% position:13%
is called
"Interrupting Whiteness

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.645
and Internalized
White Superiority."

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this just immediately
piqued my interest.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.448
I filed a records request.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:03.983
I forgot about it for
a couple of months

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.052 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then got this
trove of documents in

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.388
that was just astonishing.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.990
I've been following the
kind of conceptual ideas

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.693
of critical race theory
for the last few years,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.362
but this was the first time
I'd see it really implemented

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.198
in a way that was crystal clear,

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.366
that was extremely divisive.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.235 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then once I
released them publicly,

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.736
it kind of took on
a life of its own,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I became really
the kind of key source

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.708 line:0%
for whistleblowers
in every institution

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.210 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
in the United States,
and since then,

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.313 line:0%
I've had more than 1,000
whistleblowers contact me,

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
everything from the
smallest school districts

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.549
in middle America

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.485 align:start size:88% position:13%
to the highest levels
of the federal agencies.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.121
And they're all saying
that critical race theory

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.658 align:start position:0%
has become the dominant
ideology in these institutions.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:48.795
It's ripping us apart, but
we're scared to speak out,

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that's why we're
contacting you.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.198
- Yeah, and that's why I thought

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.300
this was such an
interesting topic

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:59.272
because for the years that
I've been doing my show,

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.507 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've had on an
awful lot of people

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.909 align:start size:84% position:16%
who have been
fighting these ideas,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.811
but there wasn't sort
of a name around it,

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.779
there wasn't like
a way to look at it

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.881 align:start size:84% position:16%
through at an
institutional level.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:84% position:16%
So when you're getting
all of these emails

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.254
from little institutions up
to the big federal stuff,

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.422
it's like I've been
seeing these emails

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.890
for the last five years,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.593
and we've been seeing Bret
Weinstein at Evergreen State,

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.762
what happened, and
Lindsay Shepherd,

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:25.198
and just the litany of examples

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.467
of people fighting this thing.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:30.803
Okay, so let's just do 101 here.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:34.407
What is critical race theory?

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:38.044
- So that's a question
with a thousand answers,

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.479
but the best that
I can describe it,

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:42.382
it's basically you take
the Marxian dichotomy

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.950
of oppressor and oppressed.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.119 align:start size:97% position:3%
So you have one group in
society that is the oppressor,

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.621
one group that is the oppressed.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.556
Traditionally, that's
been the bourgeoisie

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.758
and the proletariat.

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.693 align:start size:84% position:16%
So it's an economic
stratification.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.495
Critical race theory
basically contends

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.696
that we're going to do away

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:58.631 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the economic
categorization for now

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.534 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we're going to essentially
graft identity politics

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.770
onto this Marxian dichotomy

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.539 align:start position:0%
so that it's no longer the
bourgeoisie and the proletariat.

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.274
It's whiteness and blackness,

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:11.844
it's white Americans
versus people of color.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.279
So that's really what it is.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:16.215
It's an old Marxist idea
that's been repackaged

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:19.218 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the racial
politics of our time.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:22.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So do you see a
moment where it went

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:26.793 align:start size:88% position:13%
from an economic theory
to a racial theory?

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was there just like a
moment that that happened

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:32.999
or did it just slowly
infect the whole thing?

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I think
there's many moments.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:37.537
It's a lineage that is
a pretty long lineage,

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.939 align:start size:97% position:3%
but if you can trace it back
to the Frankfurt School,

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.741
and the Frankfurt
School theorists,

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:44.277 align:start size:81% position:19%
I guess now 50
years ago or more,

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:47.714 align:start size:97% position:3%
really realized that economic
Marxism had its limits.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.882
They realized that it
couldn't make inroads

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.517
in Europe and the United States

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we had too
big of a middle class.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.122
In the United States, you
have a suburban house,

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.591 align:start size:88% position:13%
you have an automobile,
a washing machine,

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:01.561
and people didn't really feel

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:04.464 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the oppressor/oppressed
dynamic of social class

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:06.032
was really speaking to them.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:08.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so the kind of
Marxist theoretician said,

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.536 align:start size:84% position:16%
"We're not gonna make
success that way.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:13.139
Let's figure out how we
can set up a new dynamic

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:14.674
that could be more salient."

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.709
And unfortunately, this works.

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:19.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is something that I
don't think has much basis

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.481
in reality or in fact,

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:24.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's tremendously
powerful psychologically.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.219
And you have in our elite class

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:28.521
has really adopted this rhetoric

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:31.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I think has no basis
in their daily life,

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.860
but it's become a
very potent weapon,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:36.963
a very powerful weapon
that's found resonance

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:40.400
because it combines this kind
of innate American discomfort

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.337 align:start size:97% position:3%
about race and then weaponizes
it into a political tool.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:50.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Does it strike you as
deeply anti-intellectual also?

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:53.179 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, that's the part that
is sort of amazing to me.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:57.016
When you see it seep into the
places of higher education

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:59.485
that are supposed to be
about intellectualism,

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.621 align:start size:84% position:16%
and yet they're
taking a set of ideas

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:03.756
that whittles us all
down to our skin color

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.491 align:start size:84% position:16%
as if that's the
most important thing,

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:08.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
it seems like it's
deeply anti-intellectual,

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:10.863
not actually intellectual.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.899
- Yeah, it's deeply
anti-intellectual

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:14.634
and it's frankly racist.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:15.601
I think we should call it out

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.136
for what it is.
- It's racist.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:19.906
If you look at the kind of
white supremacist ideology

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:22.775
of the 1950s, which
we all denounce,

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:24.677
it has the same categorization

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:27.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the critical race
theory ideology of today.

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:29.882 align:start size:84% position:16%
You reduce people
to a racial essence.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:33.085
Back then and today, it's
whiteness and blackness.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:36.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
You create a group
identity-based hierarchy.

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:38.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, it's different,
but it's the same concept.

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:40.793
And then these critical
race theory trainings

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:42.328 align:start size:81% position:19%
are essentially
denouncing people,

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:44.397 align:start size:88% position:13%
not on their individual
characteristics,

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:46.365
but on their inborn identity.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:49.101 align:start size:84% position:16%
This is something that
was wrong in 1950,

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:53.339 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's wrong today, and we
should be very on high alert

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:54.841
and we should all
be working together

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.843
to jettison this ideology.

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:58.845
And I think something
that's really important

00:07:58.845 --> 00:08:01.614 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that if you look
at Martin Luther King,

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.449
the kind of gold standard

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:05.318 align:start size:84% position:16%
of how we should think
about the country,

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:07.587
how we should think about race,

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:10.356
his philosophy was deeply
rooted in Christianity.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.325
He was obviously a preacher,

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.594
but it was also deeply
rooted in the Declaration

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:17.096 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the Constitution and
the work of Abraham Lincoln.

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:19.265
He was a student, you can
read this in his essays,

00:08:19.265 --> 00:08:21.267
he was a student
of American history

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:24.003
and realized that we
had to bring forward

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:26.172 align:start size:81% position:19%
the highest ideals
of the country.

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:27.540
The Black Lives Matter movement,

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.408
the critical race
theory movement,

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:32.011
they self-consciously
reject the ideology

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.479
of Martin Luther King,

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:35.781 align:start position:0%
they reject the ideology of
the Declaration of Independence

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:38.885
and they reject the ideology
of Christianity wholesale.

00:08:38.885 --> 00:08:40.720
It's a different lineage.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
It comes from the
kind of Marxist
theoreticians of the 1960s

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:48.194
and has no resonance
in our kind of organic,

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:49.795
homegrown, cultural tradition.

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:54.066
- Do you see what
they want to build

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:55.401
on the other side of this?

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.637 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's the part that
is unclear to me.

00:08:57.637 --> 00:09:00.573
I get all of the bad ideas here.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:02.108
I think a lot of my audience,

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:03.476
because we've been talking
about this stuff forever,

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:05.044
gets a lot of the bad ideas,

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:06.979 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it seems to me
that I can't really see

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:08.147
what they wanna build.

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:09.615 align:start size:84% position:16%
I can see what
they wanna destroy,

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:11.217
which is pretty much everything,

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.685
which is what we see
happening right now.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:14.020
Hollywood's crumbling,

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
our cultural institutions
are crumbling,

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:18.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
our academic institutions
are crumbling,

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
our political institutions
are crumbling.

00:09:20.026 --> 00:09:21.360
They've infected everything.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.496
So I get the destruction phase,

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:26.465
but do they even
really talk about,

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:28.100
the people that buy into this,

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.168
do they ever really talk about

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:31.237
what they will build after this?

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:33.406
I mean, is it really
going to be a world?

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:35.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
Are we going to have
anti-white laws?

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:38.744
Is that really where we're
headed with this whole thing?

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:40.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, I mean, there's two
ways to look at that question.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.815
One is you're absolutely right.

00:09:42.815 --> 00:09:44.850
Critical race theory and
critical theory in general

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.721
is not a philosophy of
substantive positive.

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:50.957
It's a philosophy
of pure negation.

00:09:50.957 --> 00:09:52.792
They're arguing that
they should deconstruct

00:09:52.792 --> 00:09:54.827
existing social institutions,

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:58.397
point out how they're kind
of coded for racial dominance

00:09:58.397 --> 00:10:00.900
and oppression, and
then obliterate them.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.435
They're not clear,

00:10:02.435 --> 00:10:04.637
and this goes back all the
way to Marx in the 1840s.

00:10:04.637 --> 00:10:07.473
Marx posited that we have
to have the revolution.

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:09.175
We have to destroy
the social order.

00:10:09.175 --> 00:10:12.144
We have to destroy all of
the kind of underpinnings

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:15.748 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
of our society, but even
Marx gave no clarity

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.950 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
on what the world
looks like after that.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.852 line:0%
It was pure utopianism.

00:10:19.852 --> 00:10:22.321 line:0%
There was no concrete
plan or development,

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:24.357
or even a vision of
what would happen.

00:10:24.357 --> 00:10:27.827
It's really this blind faith
that if you destroy what's bad,

00:10:27.827 --> 00:10:31.097 align:start size:97% position:3%
something beautiful and good
and eternal will emerge.

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:34.667
But our history in the
last 150 years globally

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:36.769 align:start size:84% position:16%
has shown that that's
absolutely wrong.

00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:38.371
When you demolish
a social order,

00:10:38.371 --> 00:10:41.707 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you empower ideologues
that divide people

00:10:41.707 --> 00:10:44.543 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the basis of group
identity, it leads to famine,

00:10:44.543 --> 00:10:46.746
it leads to war, it
leads to genocide.

00:10:46.746 --> 00:10:49.649
It leads to everything
that is bad in the world.

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:51.884 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I don't see the
critical race theorist

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:55.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
positing something
substantive in its place.

00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:57.723
And I think what
you can also see,

00:10:57.723 --> 00:10:59.225
the second way of
looking at this,

00:10:59.225 --> 00:11:03.696
is that if you look at the kind
of in practice what emerges,

00:11:03.696 --> 00:11:05.197
look at the CHAZ.

00:11:05.197 --> 00:11:07.600
You remember the Capitol Hill
Autonomous Zone in Seattle,

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.102
Black Lives Matter and
anarchists took it over.

00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:11.771 align:start size:84% position:16%
They said, "Once we
get rid of the police,

00:11:11.771 --> 00:11:13.372 align:start size:84% position:16%
once we get rid of the
Seattle government,

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:15.741
once we have our
own kind of utopia,

00:11:15.741 --> 00:11:17.176 align:start size:84% position:16%
we are going to
set up a government

00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:19.412 align:start size:84% position:16%
based on social
justice principles."

00:11:19.412 --> 00:11:21.380
And what happened?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:24.050
They set up racially
segregated facilities.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:26.619
There were meetings and
gardens and elsewhere

00:11:26.619 --> 00:11:29.488 align:start size:97% position:3%
that were explicitly
endorsing racial segregation,

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:32.358
and it devolved into
a violent nightmare.

00:11:32.358 --> 00:11:35.294
It had a homicide rate
that was 50 times greater

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:36.729
than the city of Chicago.

00:11:36.729 --> 00:11:40.833 align:start size:97% position:3%
It led to the senseless death
of African American men,

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:42.268
and it didn't work.

00:11:42.268 --> 00:11:44.704 align:start size:97% position:3%
And although that's obviously
a very small example,

00:11:44.704 --> 00:11:46.739
I think it's an important one

00:11:46.739 --> 00:11:49.408
because it gives a kind of
glimpse into what happens

00:11:49.408 --> 00:11:52.211
when you demolish law and order,

00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:54.346
when you demolish the
existing social order,

00:11:54.346 --> 00:11:57.316
and you try to replace
it with a utopian vision.

00:11:57.316 --> 00:11:59.919
- So one of the questions I
get all the time from people

00:11:59.919 --> 00:12:04.090
is they'll say, "Dave, why
is it spreading so quickly?"

00:12:05.491 --> 00:12:07.293 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's almost as if you weren't
paying attention to this,

00:12:07.293 --> 00:12:10.262 align:start size:97% position:3%
like if you weren't watching
the few YouTube channels

00:12:10.262 --> 00:12:12.998
about it or the podcasts
or whatever, you suddenly,

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:14.467
it was as if it never existed

00:12:14.467 --> 00:12:17.870 align:start position:0%
and then one day it burst
forth, and now it's everywhere.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.371
Have you thought about that?

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:23.042
Just sort of how it has been
able to spread its tentacles.

00:12:23.042 --> 00:12:25.845
so seemingly quickly,
even for the people

00:12:25.845 --> 00:12:27.313
that saw it coming for a while,

00:12:27.313 --> 00:12:30.683
it does seem like there was
suddenly like a catalyst

00:12:30.683 --> 00:12:34.420
that really exploded it
in the last six months.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:35.454
- Yeah, I think you're right,

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:36.889
and I thought a lot about that,

00:12:36.889 --> 00:12:39.024
and I'm basing it
really empirically

00:12:39.024 --> 00:12:41.227
on talking to folks
in these agencies,

00:12:41.227 --> 00:12:44.697 align:start size:97% position:3%
in these institutions, who
have been unable to resist it.

00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:47.233 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think the
explanation is really this.

00:12:47.233 --> 00:12:50.503 align:start size:97% position:3%
Critical race theory, the
intellectual argument of it,

00:12:50.503 --> 00:12:52.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
is constructed almost
like a mousetrap.

00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:55.941
It's quite ingenious, and
embedded in the premise

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:58.344
is that if you oppose
critical race theory,

00:12:58.344 --> 00:13:00.780
that's merely an expression
of your white privilege,

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.381
of your white fragility,

00:13:02.381 --> 00:13:04.383
of your internalized
white superiority,

00:13:04.383 --> 00:13:08.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they make any
resistance, any disagreement,

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:11.190 align:start size:84% position:16%
they just rationalize
that as a proof

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.692
that you are the thing that
they're fighting against.

00:13:13.692 --> 00:13:15.795
So it's constructed
in a circular way

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:18.497
where you can't truly
fight back against it.

00:13:18.497 --> 00:13:21.567
And they're using a very
kind of bare-knuckled,

00:13:21.567 --> 00:13:25.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
social shaming and social
castigation process,

00:13:25.905 --> 00:13:28.340
where if you even raise your
hand in one of these trainings

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.910 align:start size:97% position:3%
and say, "Well, you know, this
is a little bit simplistic.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.144
I see it in a more nuance way.

00:13:32.144 --> 00:13:33.979
I see it in a more complex way,"

00:13:33.979 --> 00:13:36.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're going to be berated
by at least one person

00:13:36.415 --> 00:13:38.217 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the room who
says you're a racist

00:13:38.217 --> 00:13:41.053
or a white supremacist or
a fascist or what have you.

00:13:41.053 --> 00:13:44.557
And frankly, most people who
are working a regular job,

00:13:44.557 --> 00:13:47.927 align:start size:97% position:3%
they're raising families, they
don't wanna take the risk.

00:13:47.927 --> 00:13:50.429
The social pressure
is so extraordinary

00:13:50.429 --> 00:13:52.765
that they essentially
just sit and take it.

00:13:52.765 --> 00:13:54.667
But I think what
we're finding out,

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:56.302 align:start size:81% position:19%
in the last few
months especially,

00:13:56.302 --> 00:13:58.871
