I get it, but he's
come out very strongly

00:19:25.764 --> 00:19:27.099
in the last 30 days.

00:19:27.099 --> 00:19:29.501
He's denounced critical
race theory by name,

00:19:29.501 --> 00:19:33.338 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he is the only politician
in the United States,

00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:34.940 align:start size:84% position:16%
frankly, that
would have done it.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:37.776 align:start size:84% position:16%
Jeb Bush would be
hiding under a desk.

00:19:37.776 --> 00:19:39.511
He wouldn't wanna
touch this issue.

00:19:40.979 --> 00:19:43.015 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that the
president for all of his flaws

00:19:43.015 --> 00:19:45.417
is someone who's willing
to stand against this.

00:19:45.417 --> 00:19:47.753
And you don't have
to like your allies.

00:19:47.753 --> 00:19:50.389 align:start size:97% position:3%
You just have to recognize
from a pragmatic point of view

00:19:50.389 --> 00:19:51.890 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you are fighting
the same battle

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:53.158
and when then that battle's won,

00:19:53.158 --> 00:19:55.260
you can go back to
your separate sides.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:58.363 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I think that
I've come to realize,

00:19:59.531 --> 00:20:00.999
the president has
earned my vote,

00:20:00.999 --> 00:20:03.602 align:start size:97% position:3%
specifically because of
his action on these issues.

00:20:03.602 --> 00:20:05.704
And I would encourage
folks if they have to,

00:20:05.704 --> 00:20:09.575 align:start size:88% position:13%
hold your nose and pull
down the old lever.

00:20:11.543 --> 00:20:12.978
- I'm so with you on that,

00:20:12.978 --> 00:20:16.048 align:start position:0%
and I'm glad that you explained
it as cleanly as you did,

00:20:16.048 --> 00:20:20.118 align:start position:0%
because I think the problem
with the last remaining liberals

00:20:20.118 --> 00:20:22.020
is they want to write
the Harper's letter.

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:25.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
They wanna say all the things,
address all the problems,

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:28.126
as long as they can say, "Oh,
but we don't support that guy"

00:20:28.126 --> 00:20:31.363
who's actually doing the
work to fix the thing.

00:20:31.363 --> 00:20:33.298
So can we talk about
that a little bit?

00:20:33.298 --> 00:20:36.068 align:start size:84% position:16%
That Trump is
actually doing things

00:20:36.068 --> 00:20:39.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get critical race
theory out of our system,

00:20:39.171 --> 00:20:41.707
and of course he's being
called a racist for it.

00:20:43.442 --> 00:20:45.077 align:start size:88% position:13%
You talked to Tucker
about this a little bit.

00:20:45.077 --> 00:20:47.746 align:start size:97% position:3%
Can you talk about what
Trump has actually been doing

00:20:47.746 --> 00:20:49.281
and not just talking about?

00:20:49.281 --> 00:20:51.516
The libs are all good at
talking about the things.

00:20:51.516 --> 00:20:53.852 align:start size:84% position:16%
He seems to be
actually doing things.

00:20:53.852 --> 00:20:56.555 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, the president
after following

00:20:56.555 --> 00:20:58.390
some of my reporting
on critical race theory

00:20:58.390 --> 00:20:59.958
and federal agencies,

00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:03.795
he immediately tasked his
OMB director, Russ Vought,

00:21:03.795 --> 00:21:06.598
to issue an executive
action at his request

00:21:06.598 --> 00:21:09.167
to abolish all critical
race theory trainings

00:21:09.167 --> 00:21:10.736 align:start size:84% position:16%
throughout the
federal government.

00:21:10.736 --> 00:21:12.738
This is a pretty bold move.

00:21:12.738 --> 00:21:14.172 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then he followed
it with a speech

00:21:14.172 --> 00:21:17.109 align:start size:88% position:13%
at the National Archives
where he dismembered

00:21:17.109 --> 00:21:19.645 align:start size:84% position:16%
the ideology of
critical race theory.

00:21:19.645 --> 00:21:22.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
In actually kind
of a surprisingly
intellectual dialogue

00:21:22.848 --> 00:21:24.816
where he called it out by name,

00:21:24.816 --> 00:21:26.952
he linked it to
the 1619 Project,

00:21:26.952 --> 00:21:28.720
he linked it to the
riots in the streets

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:32.157
that have been going on since
the death of George Floyd,

00:21:32.157 --> 00:21:35.294 align:start position:0%
and he says, "These are all
kind of birds of a same feather.

00:21:35.294 --> 00:21:37.963 align:start size:88% position:13%
These are all
interlinked phenomenon,

00:21:37.963 --> 00:21:39.698
and I'm gonna stand against it.

00:21:39.698 --> 00:21:41.667 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm gonna essentially
put myself in the breach

00:21:41.667 --> 00:21:44.603 align:start size:97% position:3%
and fight against it on
principle and in practice."

00:21:44.603 --> 00:21:46.705
And I think a lot of our
friends on the center left

00:21:46.705 --> 00:21:48.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
are willing to
fight in principle,

00:21:48.307 --> 00:21:50.309
but they're not willing
to fight in practice,

00:21:50.309 --> 00:21:52.444 align:start size:81% position:19%
and this is a kind
of huge error.

00:21:53.578 --> 00:21:54.780 align:start size:88% position:13%
I look at it like
this, they were saying,

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:56.214 align:start size:84% position:16%
"We don't want
Trump to fight this.

00:21:56.214 --> 00:21:58.216 align:start size:97% position:3%
We don't want him to
create this executive order

00:21:58.216 --> 00:21:59.751
banning critical race theory."

00:21:59.751 --> 00:22:01.887
And I'm saying, well, okay,
that's essentially saying

00:22:03.322 --> 00:22:06.191
we wanna keep losing, because
if we win a little bit now,

00:22:06.191 --> 00:22:08.193
there might be a backlash.

00:22:08.193 --> 00:22:10.696
That frankly is a
defeatist attitude.

00:22:10.696 --> 00:22:14.700 align:start size:84% position:16%
I find it totally
untenable on the level

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:17.803
of prudential politics, and I
would again encourage everyone

00:22:17.803 --> 00:22:19.471
to abandon that way of thinking

00:22:20.739 --> 00:22:22.474 align:start size:84% position:16%
and have some
courage and step up.

00:22:23.442 --> 00:22:24.910
- Yeah, it's one
of those things,

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:28.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
I liken it to like the
barbarians are at the gate

00:22:28.213 --> 00:22:31.183 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the one guy who's
guarding the gate still,

00:22:31.183 --> 00:22:32.818 align:start size:84% position:16%
you got all the
intellectuals going,

00:22:32.818 --> 00:22:35.554 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Ah, he talks funny
and his hair is crazy."

00:22:35.554 --> 00:22:39.124 align:start position:0%
And it's like, guys, (chuckling)
we got a bigger problem

00:22:39.124 --> 00:22:40.726
on the other side of that gate.

00:22:40.726 --> 00:22:44.629
So then after Trump
issued this speech

00:22:44.629 --> 00:22:47.566 align:start size:84% position:16%
and everything
else, then the CDC,

00:22:47.566 --> 00:22:50.068
they said they were still
gonna continue, right?

00:22:50.068 --> 00:22:52.571
But then he put an
end to that as well.

00:22:52.571 --> 00:22:54.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, it's actually
multiple federal agencies.

00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:56.875 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've reported new
whistleblower documents

00:22:56.875 --> 00:23:00.412
from the CDC, the EPA, the
Veterans Administration,

00:23:00.412 --> 00:23:01.646
and the State Department,

00:23:01.646 --> 00:23:03.215
all of which are moving forward

00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:04.916
with critical race
theory trainings,

00:23:04.916 --> 00:23:07.452
in direct violation of
a presidential order.

00:23:07.452 --> 00:23:10.322
And I think this is both a
problem substantively, right?

00:23:10.322 --> 00:23:12.424 align:start size:97% position:3%
The kind of principles
that are in these documents

00:23:12.424 --> 00:23:16.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
are divisive,
pseudo-scientific, racist,

00:23:16.061 --> 00:23:18.797 align:start size:84% position:16%
and really destructive
for the workplace.

00:23:18.797 --> 00:23:20.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it's also a
problem at the level

00:23:20.499 --> 00:23:22.234
of our constitutional system.

00:23:22.234 --> 00:23:23.735
The president is the president.

00:23:23.735 --> 00:23:25.404
He controls the agencies,

00:23:25.404 --> 00:23:27.739
and my friends and colleagues
at the Claremont Institute

00:23:27.739 --> 00:23:29.541
and elsewhere have long warned

00:23:29.541 --> 00:23:31.510
about the administrative state

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:35.113
becoming the unconstitutional
fourth branch of government.

00:23:35.113 --> 00:23:37.783
And I think this is another
illustration of that pattern

00:23:37.783 --> 00:23:41.086
where you have mid level
and even senior bureaucrats

00:23:41.086 --> 00:23:44.389
basically saying, "We can
openly defy the president.

00:23:44.389 --> 00:23:46.992
We're gonna do what we want,
even though nobody elected us,

00:23:46.992 --> 00:23:49.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we don't have this
power in the Constitution,

00:23:49.461 --> 00:23:50.962
we're gonna keep doing it."

00:23:50.962 --> 00:23:54.199 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I think in the short
term, this is not a big deal.

00:23:54.199 --> 00:23:56.835 align:start size:84% position:16%
The OMB director
will shut these down.

00:23:56.835 --> 00:23:59.971
But in the long term, on the
kind of theoretical basis,

00:23:59.971 --> 00:24:01.506
this is a major problem.

00:24:01.506 --> 00:24:03.842
You have an administrative state

00:24:03.842 --> 00:24:07.179 align:start size:88% position:13%
that essentially
doesn't think of itself

00:24:07.179 --> 00:24:09.281
as beholden to the
political order.

00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:10.982
and I think that
is a huge problem

00:24:10.982 --> 00:24:13.785
and we've gotta tackle
that when the time comes.

00:24:13.785 --> 00:24:16.455
- In effect, you're talking
about the deep state there

00:24:16.455 --> 00:24:17.656 align:start size:84% position:16%
when you say the
administrative state.

00:24:17.656 --> 00:24:18.924
Do you make a distinction

00:24:18.924 --> 00:24:21.226
or you just don't
like that phrase?

00:24:21.226 --> 00:24:23.228 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I think I
don't like the phrase.

00:24:23.228 --> 00:24:26.298
I think there's a really
strong body of scholarship

00:24:26.298 --> 00:24:28.366
on the phrase, the
administrative state.

00:24:28.366 --> 00:24:31.403 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think the deep state
can kind of verge

00:24:31.403 --> 00:24:33.505
into conspiratorial territory.

00:24:33.505 --> 00:24:36.942
So it's a personal choice, but
I think administrative state

00:24:36.942 --> 00:24:40.178
is on much more solid
intellectual footing,

00:24:40.178 --> 00:24:44.282
and we have a long list of folks

00:24:44.282 --> 00:24:46.218
who have done the background,

00:24:46.218 --> 00:24:48.687
done the homework,
done the reading,

00:24:48.687 --> 00:24:51.723
that I would encourage
everyone to look up.

00:24:51.723 --> 00:24:54.559
- So let's say through
this executive action,

00:24:54.559 --> 00:24:58.797
Trump is able to get this stuff
out of the federal agencies.

00:24:58.797 --> 00:25:00.899
It sounds like it's still
gonna be a fight to do so

00:25:00.899 --> 00:25:02.567
and who knows if that's
even really possible,

00:25:02.567 --> 00:25:05.937 align:start size:88% position:13%
but let's just say that
that kind of works.

00:25:05.937 --> 00:25:07.706
Are you worried then
that what will happen

00:25:07.706 --> 00:25:09.374
is we'll have federal agencies

00:25:09.374 --> 00:25:12.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
that will have
removed this stuff,

00:25:12.244 --> 00:25:15.981
but in effect, we'll just have
all the private institutions,

00:25:15.981 --> 00:25:19.451
the private schools,
all of our businesses,

00:25:19.451 --> 00:25:21.753 align:start size:88% position:13%
our television networks,
all of these things,

00:25:21.753 --> 00:25:23.522
they will still be infected,

00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:26.258
and that infection will
almost create a situation

00:25:26.258 --> 00:25:28.426 align:start size:97% position:3%
where the federal government
will be unable to operate

00:25:28.426 --> 00:25:31.296
because the outside forces

00:25:31.296 --> 00:25:33.265
won't let the federal government

00:25:33.265 --> 00:25:36.401 align:start size:97% position:3%
do what it's supposed to do,
something to that effect.

00:25:36.401 --> 00:25:40.605 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, I would kind of
contextualize it in this way.

00:25:40.605 --> 00:25:42.440
I think we've long been
concerned about this

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:44.175
for the last few years,

00:25:44.175 --> 00:25:45.677
but this is the first time

00:25:45.677 --> 00:25:47.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we've actually gotten
anything done about it.

00:25:47.245 --> 00:25:48.647 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it's really
substantively

00:25:48.647 --> 00:25:50.148
the first successful pushback

00:25:50.148 --> 00:25:52.217 align:start size:97% position:3%
against critical race
theory in our institutions,

00:25:52.217 --> 00:25:53.652
but it's not the first.

00:25:53.652 --> 00:25:56.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is really the opening
shot in a long war.

00:25:56.221 --> 00:25:58.557 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that we can
start with federal agencies.

00:25:58.557 --> 00:26:00.825
We can start with other
public institutions.

00:26:00.825 --> 00:26:03.862
We can kind of shut off
the spigot of funding

00:26:03.862 --> 00:26:06.197
that goes towards the
university programs

00:26:06.197 --> 00:26:09.067
that are creating this
intellectual framework.

00:26:09.067 --> 00:26:11.369 align:start size:84% position:16%
We can go after local
school districts

00:26:11.369 --> 00:26:14.039
and local institutions
that are funding this.

00:26:14.039 --> 00:26:16.308
And then what we do is
we change the calculation

00:26:16.308 --> 00:26:19.110 align:start size:97% position:3%
for corporations that I think
will adapt very quickly.

00:26:19.110 --> 00:26:21.246
What we need to do is we
need to raise the cost

00:26:21.246 --> 00:26:23.982 align:start size:88% position:13%
of doing these programs,
because right now

00:26:23.982 --> 00:26:26.851
the kind of risk management
protocol for corporations

00:26:26.851 --> 00:26:29.888 align:start size:97% position:3%
is, well, we really don't
lose anything by doing this,

00:26:29.888 --> 00:26:32.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we insulate ourselves
against the attack

00:26:32.123 --> 00:26:34.092
of being a big, bad corporation.

00:26:34.092 --> 00:26:36.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so what they're doing
is they're protecting

00:26:36.461 --> 00:26:40.865
their economic prospects
with our existing policies,

00:26:40.865 --> 00:26:43.168
and this is a way
of risk management

00:26:43.168 --> 00:26:47.572
for their social policies and
social status in the world.

00:26:47.572 --> 00:26:50.609 align:start size:97% position:3%
What we have to do is we
have to change that formula,

00:26:50.609 --> 00:26:53.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
where we significantly
escalate the cost

00:26:53.311 --> 00:26:54.613
of doing these programs.

00:26:54.613 --> 00:26:56.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think the
next step is clearly

00:26:57.816 --> 00:27:01.186 align:start position:0%
a kind of campaign of legal
warfare against these programs.

00:27:01.186 --> 00:27:03.922
Peter Kirsanow and others
have argued persuasively

00:27:03.922 --> 00:27:06.992
that these constitute
workplace harassment,

00:27:06.992 --> 00:27:10.028
that these violate the
Equal Protection Clause

00:27:10.028 --> 00:27:11.563
and the Civil Rights Act.

00:27:11.563 --> 00:27:12.964 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I think that's
the next step.

00:27:12.964 --> 00:27:15.600
And I really think
that I'm excited,

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:18.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm energized by
this initial victory.

00:27:18.203 --> 00:27:19.437
We have a long way to go,

00:27:19.437 --> 00:27:21.373
but I think that if
we work together,

00:27:21.373 --> 00:27:23.074
we get our heads
out of the clouds

00:27:23.074 --> 00:27:27.746
and we actually fight, kind
of swords out on the ground,

00:27:27.746 --> 00:27:28.980
I think we can win this

00:27:28.980 --> 00:27:30.915
because I think the vast
majority of Americans,

00:27:30.915 --> 00:27:34.219
if they actually find
out what this theory

00:27:34.219 --> 00:27:38.356
is advocating for, would
wholeheartedly reject it.

00:27:38.356 --> 00:27:40.291
- Yeah, I'm with you, man.

00:27:40.291 --> 00:27:43.495 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you think that there's sort
of a micro way of fighting

00:27:43.495 --> 00:27:44.996
and a macro way of fighting?

00:27:44.996 --> 00:27:47.766 align:start size:97% position:3%
So it sounds like Trump and
what you just described there,

00:27:47.766 --> 00:27:49.601
that's sort of the macro level.

00:27:49.601 --> 00:27:51.102
We have to fight it at
the governmental level.

00:27:51.102 --> 00:27:53.605 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
But one of the questions
I get all the time,

00:27:53.605 --> 00:27:56.274 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
especially from
college people is,

00:27:56.274 --> 00:27:58.243 line:0%
well, how do I fight
it just personally

00:27:58.243 --> 00:28:01.913 align:start size:97% position:3%
if one of my friends has
been just wholly brainwashed

00:28:01.913 --> 00:28:03.348
by this set of ideas?

00:28:03.348 --> 00:28:05.316
And I don't know that
there's a great answer.

00:28:05.316 --> 00:28:08.353
I'll tell them, well, you can
share some Prager U videos

00:28:08.353 --> 00:28:12.323
or listen to Larry Elder or
read a book by Thomas Sowell,

00:28:12.323 --> 00:28:14.793 align:start size:84% position:16%
but that's sort of
all intellectual
stuff in a certain way

00:28:14.793 --> 00:28:17.962 align:start size:88% position:13%
that often you're not
gonna get younger people

00:28:17.962 --> 00:28:19.397
to take the time to do.

00:28:20.532 --> 00:28:22.400 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you have any tricks
on the micro level

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:24.836 align:start size:84% position:16%
on how to wake
people up about this?

00:28:24.836 --> 00:28:26.071
- No, I don't.

00:28:26.071 --> 00:28:28.339
Actually, I've come to
the personal conclusion

00:28:28.339 --> 00:28:30.875 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the kind of
micro level one-on-one

00:28:30.875 --> 00:28:32.143
is probably a waste of time.

00:28:32.143 --> 00:28:34.245
You find yourself
debating some dude

00:28:34.245 --> 00:28:36.414
you went to high school with
on a long Facebook thread.

00:28:36.414 --> 00:28:37.682
It never goes anywhere.

00:28:37.682 --> 00:28:39.184
I think that this
is really at heart

00:28:39.184 --> 00:28:40.485
an institutional battle.

00:28:40.485 --> 00:28:42.020
You have to win it
institutionally.

00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:44.155 align:start size:84% position:16%
So rather than arguing
with your roommate,

00:28:44.155 --> 00:28:47.859
you should be waging a kind
of sophisticated campaign

00:28:47.859 --> 00:28:50.028
against the dean of your school.

00:28:50.028 --> 00:28:51.696
And I think that's
the way to do it.

00:28:51.696 --> 00:28:53.565
I think that, unfortunately,

00:28:53.565 --> 00:28:57.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're in this really awful
political environment

00:28:57.268 --> 00:29:00.238 align:start position:0%
where in order to maintain
kind of one-on-one friendships,

00:29:00.238 --> 00:29:02.907
sometimes you just have to
put politics off the table.

00:29:02.907 --> 00:29:06.244
So I think, again, it's
an institutional fight

00:29:06.244 --> 00:29:09.080
and that's really where the
most progress can be made.

00:29:09.080 --> 00:29:11.049
- Yeah, so I said to you
right before we started

00:29:11.049 --> 00:29:13.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I wanted to keep this
exactly to a half hour,

